  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Adjetivos de personalidad**",
      "",
      "| Positivo | Matiz | Negativo / contrario |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| *outgoing* | sociable | *shy* (tímido), *reserved* (reservado) |",
      "| *reliable* | de fiar | *unreliable* |",
      "| *generous* | da sin esperar nada | *mean* (tacaño) |",
      "| *determined* | decidido | *stubborn* (terco) |",
      "| *easy-going* | tranquilo | *bossy* (mandón), *moody* (de humor cambiante) |",
      "| *patient* | paciente | *impatient* |",
      "| *honest* | sincero | *dishonest* |",
      "",
      "**Prefijos negativos:** *un-* (unreliable, unfriendly, unkind) · *im-* delante de **p** y **m** (impatient, impolite, immature) · *in-* (insecure, inconsiderate) · *dis-* (dishonest, disloyal).",
      "",
      "**Frases útiles para describir**",
      "",
      "- *He's the kind of person who …* (Es de esos que…) → *She's the kind of person who always helps.*",
      "- *He tends to + verbo* (suele, tiende a) → *He tends to be late.*",
      "- *I'd describe myself as …* → *I'd describe myself as quite outgoing.*",
      "- *quite, a bit, rather, really, extremely* suavizan o refuerzan: *a bit stubborn · extremely generous*.",
      "- *can be + adjetivo* (a veces es…): *He can be moody.*",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** *stubborn* es negativo y *determined* es positivo, aunque describan algo parecido. *Sympathetic* no es 'simpático': es 'comprensivo, compasivo'. *Sensible* no es 'sensible': es 'sensato'.",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *generous* /ˈdʒenərəs/ (3 sílabas) · *ambitious* /æmˈbɪʃəs/ · *reliable* /rɪˈlaɪəbl/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "He is very sympathetic.",
        "right": "He is very nice / friendly.",
        "note": "Sympathetic = comprensivo, no simpático."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "She's unpatient.",
        "right": "She's impatient.",
        "note": "Im- delante de p y m."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": [
      {
        "word": "sympathetic",
        "es_false": "simpático",
        "real": "comprensivo, compasivo",
        "note": "'Simpático' se dice nice o friendly."
      },
      {
        "word": "sensible",
        "es_false": "sensible",
        "real": "sensato",
        "note": "'Sensible' se dice sensitive."
      }
    ]
  },
